User requested cause analysis/custom solution for crawl. Latest four logs show zero character packs, all four framework plugin mains complete,3704 shader pipelines in24532ms,30 presentation windows ranging0.149-15.187FPS, no guest-exception,247 file-size patch warnings even with no packs. Journal640142bytes/3916events (2603 engine warnings,1270guest-debug) over first161.696s; frame reporting continues as journal quiets. Do not blame Infernape for those247 warnings or declare plugin-specific root cause from these logs. Identified avoidable overhead in our diagnostic code: journal did stat/open/write/close per record and Smash forced engine per-line flushing. Runtime6cd74e1 batches normal journal records via existing one-second LogFlusher, uses separate producer/I/O locks,256KiB pending threshold applies backpressure, guest fault/durable markers synchronously drain/fsync; explicit immediate mode preserved. Normal native-signal/kill/power-loss tails can now lose recent buffered records (longer if storage stalls); don't promise lossless crash logs. Removes forced Smash engine line flush. Adds every-five-second release Smash counters and CPU owner snapshots (heap.log), timers_on for focused Smash profiling; counter overlap/unsupported/stale sampling and GPU-worker idle-vs-hardware meaning documented. Native initial1b7db5d compile found out-of-scope title bool in release-only path; fixed6cd74e1 uses loaded system title. Host1b runtime batching code builds; real guest fault preserved preceding batched warnings/debug/context (results/guest-diagnostics-eq8o33ja). New real blocked-write test proves producers enqueue while storage stalled;200records onebatch, immediate/periodic/Stop flushing, durability, rotation, bounds pass. Collector2tests and crash-report retention tests pass. No measured PS5 speedup/root cause yet.

